TIP:  For the opening, form up (G) and pick the open 4th string <d>, then lay flat whichever finger you use to play the 5th string of the (G) onto the 5th string to briefly fret the 4th string <e>, and then lift up and pick the open 3rd string <g> and strum (G).  The sequence of chords moves quickly.  

TIP:  That same sequence in the intro is played as a fiddle voicing that enters right after “ . . . (D) down in Mary’s (G) Land.”  The (G) is the last chord on “Land” followed immediately by an (Em) so don’t dawdle – proceed immediately from the trailing (G) to that first (Em) or you’ll be caught out.

 
